      "comment": "Traupman’s word for a pastry shop (129, 131). Classically it is a craving for delicacies, or a titbit; the market in Rome where delicacies were sold was <span lang=\"la\">forum cuppēdinis</span> (Varr. LL 5.146, Lewis &amp; Short). We have found no ancient instance of it for a shop.",
